{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The end of an ending that concludes with a downward jog, as is typical for first endings.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue\/stop","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLStartStopDiscontinueO4stopyA2CmF","symbolKind":"case","title":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue.stop","roleHeading":"Case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stop"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stop"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue\/stop"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStopDiscontinue/stop":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue\/stop","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue\/stop","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stop"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The end of an ending that concludes with a downward jog, as is typical for first endings.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue.stop"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStopDiscontinue":{"title":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue","abstract":[{"text":"The start-stop-discontinue type is used to specify ending types. Typically, the start type is associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a downward","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is typical for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"second endings that do not conclude a piece.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue"}]}}}